            <ArticleTitle>Clinical evaluation of a patient presenting with headache.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>847-63, v</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Evaluation of the headache patient requires a reasonable history and physical examination supported by some knowledge of common headache disorders and their presentations. The diagnostician requires the ability to recognize serious headache disorders based on a working knowledge of the principles of clinical neurology. This article outlines the salient points to consider in the process of headache assessment, based on a clinical overview analysis of the characteristics of several headache disorders.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
